<github-data-json>
{
  "title": "Defects D0b: land checks and post-merge gates record classified failure observations",
  "body": "## Problem\nPart of #823, slice D0b. Blocked by #933 (D0a).\n\nD0a records a run's gates only. Land checks and post-merge gates still leave their failures in prose: `land_entries.reason` and land events (`src/land/queue.ts:884-920`), and `coordinatorConfirmation.reason` (`post-merge-confirmation.ts:25-160`). So D1 can't see land or post-merge failures, and `platform` (a worker failure that a different-OS coordinator confirmation passes) can't be classified at all.\n\n- **Land.** Every claim increments `attempts` and re-runs the checks from the start (`src/db/store.ts:3270-3274`, `queue.ts:437`). Executions run through `executeGate` inside `LandQueue.checks`, not through `runGateExecution`.\n- **Post-merge.**\n  - `isSlowRegression` (`src/gates/run.ts:560-575`) requires an unretried result, and is evaluated as `retryRegressions`'s selector (`engine.ts:3471`), before the re-check replaces `c.result`.\n  - A slow regression whose re-check fails can then still pass coordinator confirmation (`engine.ts:3457-3499`, `post-merge-confirmation.ts:25-160`).\n  - `confirmPostMerge` keeps the worker's original failure in `firstAttempt` or `coordinatorConfirmation`, and the coordinator's passing result in `c.result` (`post-merge-confirmation.ts:137-146`).\n\n## Invariant\nD0a's invariant extended to:\n- **Land checks:** the primary execution of each land claim attempt, keyed by `(land entry id, attempts, phase, name)`;\n- **Post-merge gates:** the primary execution of each post-merge attempt (purpose `rebase`), keyed by D0a's execution identity.\n\nThe same table, fields, classifier, signature, promotion and finalization rules apply. In addition:\n- `platform` is assigned only when the worker's and the coordinator's captured OS are both known and differ.\n- The slow-regression predicate is captured before any re-check replaces the result.\n\n## Requirements\n1. **Land.**\n   - In `LandQueue.checks`, record the primary `executeGate` result's failures before retries, through D0a's insert helper.\n   - Location: the land's gate executor (coordinator, or the LAN worker by D0a's rule, with `worker_os`).\n   - Finalize when `checks` decides (blocked, or passed with flaky retries), in the same transaction as the land entry's update.\n   - A claim lost mid-check leaves its attempt's rows unfinalized until the entry reaches `landed`, `blocked` or `cancelled`. They are then finalized as `interrupted`. The next claim's attempt is a new execution with new rows.\n2. **Post-merge.**\n   - Record the failures of the post-merge primary execution through D0a's checkpoint (stage `gates`, purpose `rebase`).\n   - Store `slow_regression`, the `isSlowRegression` value computed by `retryRegressions`'s selector at `engine.ts:3471`, on the observation before the re-check.\n   - Finalize after `confirmPostMerge`, in the transaction that saves `post-merge-confirmed`.\n   - History gains `confirmed_passed`, `confirmed_failed` and `confirmation_unavailable`. A slow regression's re-check sets `retry_passed` or `retry_failed`, as in D0a.\n3. **Classifier rows,** inserted into D0a's table after row 2, in this order:\n\n   | # | Observation and history | Class |\n   |---|---|---|\n   | 2a | `slow_regression` with `retry_passed` (the re-check passed) | `load` |\n   | 2b | `confirmed_passed`, with both OS values known and different | `platform` |\n   | 2c | `confirmed_passed`, with both OS values known and equal | `flaky` |\n   | 2d | `confirmed_passed`, with either OS unknown | `unclassified`, reason \"worker OS unknown\". A legacy unknown OS never establishes `platform`. |\n   | 2e | `confirmed_failed` | `regression` |\n   | 2f | `confirmation_unavailable` | `unclassified`, keeping the reason as evidence |\n\n   The combined history of a slow regression whose re-check failed (`retry_failed`) and whose coordinator confirmation then passed matches 2b, 2c or 2d, not 2a. Its `slow_regression` flag stays as evidence.\n\n## Tests\nEach must fail without its change.\n1. **Land setup.** A land check blocked by a failing setup step is `setup`, keyed by entry and attempt. A re-claimed entry's next attempt adds new rows, and the lost attempt is finalized as `interrupted` when the entry ends.\n2. **Land retries.** A land check that passes on its targeted retry is `flaky`; one with a rejected retry is `regression`.\n3. **Post-merge confirmation.**\n   - A Linux worker failure that a macOS coordinator confirmation passes is `platform`.\n   - On the same OS it is `flaky`.\n   - A legacy job with no `worker_os` is `unclassified` (\"worker OS unknown\").\n   - A coordinator failure is `regression`.\n   - An expired confirmation deadline is `unclassified`, with the reason.\n4. **Slow regressions.**\n   - A slow regression whose re-check passes is `load`.\n   - **Combined history:** a slow regression whose re-check fails and whose coordinator confirmation passes is `platform`, `flaky` or `unclassified` by the OS rule, with `slow_regression` kept in the evidence.\n   - The predicate was captured before the re-check.\n5. **Signature.** It comes from the worker's failed attempt, not the coordinator's passing result.\n6. **Restart.** A post-merge gate resumed after its observation and before the `post-merge-confirmed` save ends finalized exactly once.\n\n## Compatibility\nAs D0a. There's no new table. Land entry updates are unchanged, apart from running in a transaction with the finalization.\n\n## Out of scope\nAs D0a, minus land and post-merge.\n\n## Budget\nAbout 115 changed source lines plus tests: land ~45, post-merge ~40, classifier rows ~30. Stop at 155 and report.\n"
}
</github-data-json>
