 {
  "id": "F1",
  "file": "src/db/failure-observations.ts",
  "line": 104,
  "title": "Post-merge: an execution that passes after a restart keeps the earlier failure's flaky class",
  "detail": "Earlier-stage retry history is enabled only for `purpose === \"initial\"` (~104). A local post-merge execution that fails, records its observation, then restarts before confirmation and passes under a fresh execution finalizes the row as `unclassified / no_retry` instead of `flaky / retry_passed`.\nExtend D0a's earlier-stage handling to rebase (post-merge) observations. Reproduced by the added pipeline-gates regression below."
 },
 {
  "id": "F2",
  "file": "src/pipeline/engine.ts",
  "line": 3514,
  "title": "Slow-regression evidence: match observations by durable execution identity, not the new stage row",
  "detail": "The selector (~3514) picks observations by the current stage-row ID. A restart creates a new stage row, while the idempotent insert keeps the observation's original stage ID. The selector computes `true`, but the update (~3573) touches no row, so a failed slow re-check followed by a passing confirmation keeps `slow_regression = 0` for a replayed LAN execution.\nMatch on the durable execution identity (handle and attempt). Reproduced by the LAN variant of the same regression."
 },
 {
  "id": "F3",
  "file": "src/land/queue.ts",
  "line": 930,
  "title": "Land retries: derive the comparison verdict from the effective retry result, so confinement wins",
  "detail": "Every final land comparison's verdict is hardcoded to `regressed` (~930). When the primary check fails ordinarily and its targeted retry hits a confinement failure, the shared classifier never sees the `confinement_error` verdict it needs (src/gates/failure-class.ts ~70). The observation becomes `regression / retry_failed`, although D0a requires `confinement`. Landing still blocks; the recorded class is wrong.\nDerive the verdict from the effective retry result. Reproduced by the added land-queue regression.\n\nScope: the change is 260 source lines against the spec's ~115 (stop at 155). Keep this round to these three fixes and report the final count.\n\nRegressions (all fail at HEAD), for test/pipeline-gates.test.ts and test/land-queue.test.ts:\n```ts\n\ntest(\"land observation classifies a confined targeted retry as confinement\", async () => {\n  const { pr } = await retryLandFixture();\n  const fake = fakeLandGates((req, attempt) =>\n    retryRun(req, {\n      test: attempt === 1 ? testFailure : { ok: false, exitCode: 1, confinementError: true },\n    }),\n  );\n  const entry = await queue({ gateExecutor: fake.executor }).request({ target: pr.run.id });\n  await settle();\n  expect(store.getLandEntry(entry.id)?.state).toBe(\"blocked\");\n  expect(store.failureObservations()).toHaveLength(1);\n  expect(store.failureObservations()[0]).toMatchObject({\n    class: \"confinement\",\n    history: \"retry_failed\",\n    finalized_at: expect.any(Number),\n  });\n});\n\ntest.each([\"local\", \"lan\"])(\n  \"post-merge observation survives restart immediately after evidence (%s)\",\n  async (kind) => {\n    writeFileSync(\n      join(repoDir, \".limitless.toml\"),\n      '[gates]\\nretry_files = \"bun test {files}\"\\nchecks = [{ name = \"test\", run = \"bun test\" }]\\n',\n    );\n    await sh([\"git\", \"commit\", \"-qam\", \"early restart fixture\"], { cwd: repoDir });\n    const bare = await githubFixture();\n    const f = start(async (s) => {\n      if (roleOf(s) === \"triage\") return { structured: triage({ suggested_profile: \"quick\" }) };\n      if (roleOf(s) === \"review\") {\n        await advanceBase(bare, \"base.txt\", \"base\\n\");\n        return { structured: approve };\n      }\n      return { files: { \"farewell.txt\": \"goodbye\\n\" } };\n    });\n    await f.stop();\n    registerGithub(f, bare);\n    const fixture = postMergeWorkerFixture(f, kind === \"local\" ? \"local\" : \"pass\");\n    const executor = f.deps.gateExecutor;\n    if (!executor) throw new Error(\"missing executor\");\n    let failures = 0;\n    f.deps.gateExecutor = {\n      ...executor,\n      attach(...args) {\n        const execution = executor.attach(...args);\n        return {\n          ...execution,\n          result: execution.result.then((result) => {\n            if (kind !== \"local\" || result.checks.every((r) => r.ok) || ++failures === 1) return result;\n            return {\n              ...result,\n              checks: result.checks.map((r) => ({ ...r, ok: true, exitCode: 0, output: \"pass\" })),\n            };\n          }),\n        };\n      },\n    };\n    f.deps.faults = {\n      \"store:save\": {\n        action: \"throw\",\n        when: (c) =>\n          c.checkpoint === \"gate-result\" && f.store.failureObservations().some((r) => r.purpose === \"rebase\"),\n      },\n    };\n    try {\n      const run = await f.createRun({ repo: \"test/repo\", prompt: \"Add farewell\", profile: \"quick\" });\n      expect(await executeRun(f.deps, run.id, new AbortController().signal)).toBe(\"queued\");\n      const before = f.store.failureObservations().filter((r) => r.purpose === \"rebase\");\n      expect(before).toHaveLength(1);\n      expect(before[0]?.finalized_at).toBeNull();\n      expect(await executeRun(f.deps, run.id, new AbortController().signal)).toBe(\"succeeded\");\n      const after = f.store.failureObservations().filter((r) => r.purpose === \"rebase\");\n      expect(after).toHaveLength(1);\n      expect(after[0]?.id).toBe(before[0]?.id);\n      expect(after[0]?.finalized_at).toBeNumber();\n      if (kind === \"local\") expect(after[0]).toMatchObject({ class: \"flaky\", history: \"retry_passed\" });\n      else expect(after[0]).toMatchObject({ slow_regression: 1, history: \"confirmed_passed\" });\n    } finally {\n      fixture.processSpy.mockRestore();\n    }\n  },\n);\n\n```"
 }
